Package: xsnip
Architecture: any
Depends: ${shlibs:Depends}, ${misc:Depends}
Description: screenshot tool with a minimal markup editor (X11)
 xsnip grabs the whole screen or a mouse-selected region and opens a small
 editor window on top of it: a pen and a text tool, five colours, and sizes
 expressed as a percentage of the smaller image side, so a stroke looks the
 same on 800x600 and on 4K.
 .
 Clicking "done" copies the result to the clipboard (served by a forked X11
 selection owner, so it survives the process) or writes it to a PNG file.
 Window type and position can be chosen for tiling window managers: the
 dialog type stays floating in i3 and honours the requested corner.
 .
 Built directly on Xlib and Xft, with no toolkit dependency.
